\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Eternal Father, strong to save,
\par Whose arm doth  bind the restless wave,
\par Who bidd'st the mighty ocean deep
\par Its own appointed limits keep:
\par O hear us when we cry to Thee
\par For those in peril on the sea!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O Saviour, whose almighty word
\par The winds and waves submissive heard,
\par Who walkedst on the foaming deep,
\par And calm amid its rage didst sleep:
\par O hear us when we cry to Thee
\par For those in peril on the sea!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Sacred Spirit, who didst brood
\par Upon the chaos dark and rude,
\par Who bad'st its angry tumult cease,
\par And gavest light, and life, and peace:
\par O hear us when we cry to Thee
\par For those in peril on the sea!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O Trinity of love and power,
\par Our brethren shield in danger's hour;
\par From rock and tempest, fire and foe,
\par Protect them wheresoe'er they  go;
\par And ever let there rise to Thee
\par Glad hymns of praise from land and sea.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

